# git-secrets false-positive allowlist (extended regexes, matched per line).
#
# Real xAI API keys carry a fixed lowercase prefix, so the pattern that catches
# them also matches ordinary hyphenated identifiers that share it: this repo's
# own plugin name and directory path, and xAI's package names.
#
# Every entry is anchored with a trailing `([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)` so it matches only
# the exact identifier followed by a delimiter or end of line. A real key, whose
# random suffix runs straight on from the prefix with no delimiter, does NOT
# match. Unanchored substrings would have exempted any key beginning with those
# characters, which is the bug this shape fixes.
#
# git-secrets exempts the WHOLE LINE when an allowed pattern matches it, so
# entries must be as narrow as possible. The websocket subprotocol entry below is
# therefore pinned to the literal documentation placeholder, complete with its
# `{TOKEN}` stand-in, rather than the bare header name: that header carries a live
# ephemeral token in real code, and exempting the bare name would let an actual
# secret through on that line.
#
# That last entry writes its own prefix with a one-character class so the line is
# regex-equivalent but is not itself literal key-shaped text, which would
# otherwise make this file trip the very hook it configures.
xai-voice([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-sdk-python([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-sdk-go([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-proto([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-org([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-go([^A-Za-z0-9_/-]|$)
xai-[c]lient-secret\.\{TOKEN\}
